wner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-22T20:22:16Z","updated_at":"2021-06-22T20:22:16Z","body":"> if you function does not have dynamic arguments, you can wrap the function in a computed\r\n\r\nYeah, but if it has and they come from `v-for` (like in the example in my comment in the mentioned commit) i can't use computed.\r\nI wonder why do we even need this check, vue doesn't check if you have proper expression in `v-bind:foo` or in mustaches, you're just getting a syntax or runtime error, why it's not enough in `v-model`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/866306906/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jacekkarczmarczyk","id":15625235,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjI1MjM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15625235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk","html_url":"https://github.com/jacekkarczmarczyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacekkarczmarczyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users